From b1ed32ea386011d9b9518abee7217dd780ad90bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yu Watanabe <watanabe.yu+github@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:42:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] socket-util: harden some helpers (#44951)

Combined backport of PR #44951, which consists of the following commits:

  c0fbedf7aeac9649783984e277c2d3848cffeadf socket-util: also compare ports in sockaddr_equal()
  187673da46e2b206b83f26857175b6bf4aa6889a socket-util: refuse truncated source addresses in recvmsg_safe()
  a10cac898fb03f813f1cb80a0e71bb395eb0f8b5 socket-util: drop datagrams from port 0 in recvmsg_safe()
  b1ed32ea386011d9b9518abee7217dd780ad90bb socket-util: harden some helpers (#44951)

sockaddr_equal() so far only compared the addresses of AF_INET/AF_INET6/
AF_VSOCK socket addresses, but ignored the port. Compare the port too.

recvmsg_safe() now also refuses source addresses that the kernel silently
truncated (msg_namelen reports the full size, no flag is set), and
suppresses AF_INET/AF_INET6 datagrams coming from source port 0, which are
never legitimate. Raw IP sockets have no concept of ports, hence a new
recvmsg_safe_full() with RECVMSG_SAFE_ALLOW_PORT_ZERO is introduced and
icmp6_receive() uses it.

[v255 backport note: this tree is v255.2 and its recvmsg_safe() predates
several later upstream changes, so the hunks were re-adapted:
 - v255.2 recvmsg_safe() only checks MSG_CTRUNC (not MSG_TRUNC/-ECHRNG, from
   commit ad501930d749) and does not retry without MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC (commit
   cd3e6e7984b4); those parts were not added, the function keeps the v255.2
   recvmsg() call and CTRUNC handling.
 - src/basic/socket-util.c did not include "in-addr-util.h", which is needed
   for in6_addr_equal(); the include was added.
 - v255.2 src/test/test-socket-util.c has neither ASSERT_OK*/ASSERT_ERROR*
   nor ASSERT_STREQ()/ASSERT_GT() macros and no TEST(recvmsg_safe_packet)
   anchor, so the new tests use assert_se()/streq() and are inserted before
   TEST(receive_nopassfd); FOREACH_ARGUMENT() does not exist either and was
   replaced by an explicit array loop. The tests only cover the behaviour
   added here, not the MSG_TRUNC case from ad501930d749.]
